Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: pngset.c
Line: 1418
Function: png_ensure_fcTL_is_valid
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: The check 'if (width + x_offset > png_ptr->first_frame_width || height + y_offset > png_ptr->first_frame_height)' performs 32-bit additions on png_uint_32 values. If width or x_offset (or height/y_offset) are large (up to PNG_UINT_31_MAX), the addition can overflow and wrap, causing the oversized-frame validation to be bypassed. This can allow an invalid APNG frame that extends beyond the first frame to be accepted, potentially leading to out-of-bounds accesses during subsequent frame composition.

